    "durationMs": 236794,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Implementation** (NestJS 11.2.11 + TypeORM 0.3 on PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`):\n- `src/links/` — `Link` entity (serial id, unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, `created_at`), service, controller\n- `src/migrations/` — TypeORM migration creating the `links` table with a unique index on `code`\n- `src/common/all-exceptions.filter.ts` — global filter returning `{\"error\": …}` JSON; maps body-parser's malformed-JSON 400 to 422\n- `src/data-source.ts` — DataSource built from `DATABASE_URL` (never hard-coded), used by `typeorm migration:run`\n- `start.sh` — builds, applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on **0.0.0.0:8000** (verified binding via /proc/net/tcp)\n- `README.md` — includes a \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Verified against the spec:**\n- `POST /links`: 201 with `{\"code\", \"url\", \"clicks\": 0}`; generated 8-char codes; URL returned unchanged; missing/invalid `url` (non-http(s), no host, non-string), invalid `code` (too short/long/bad chars), and malformed JSON → 422; duplicate custom code → 409\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200 with all fields; unknown → 404 with error field\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with correct `Location`; 20 concurrent redirects yielded `clicks: 20` exactly (atomic `clicks + 1` UPDATE…RETURNING)\n- `GET /links` → `{\"items\": [...], \"total\"}` in ascending creation order\n- Restarted the server via `sh start.sh` — links and click counts survived; migrations are idempotent on re-run\n\nOne environment quirk worth noting: npm silently failed to extract `@types/*` packages into this workspace's node_modules, so I installed them into a scratch dir and copied them in — the build compiles cleanly now. I also left the database truncated so the test suite starts with clean data, and stopped my test server."
  }
